96cc1d-a1a7-4ccd-bef1-5f9162d6115e","position":{"commit_sha":"5fe47ccca1a91899affc4a34c06a4d37c3551dd4","position":"1787375935308931001-7c96cc1d-a1a7-4ccd-bef1-5f9162d6115e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"375699b79bf1eadcb3452e93f419c057e6b4a23498522e4b8496af440358529a","event_uuid":"bbd16ea0-610a-44f8-91d7-aa0aefb7eaa9","position":{"commit_sha":"76d7586a19f75f5a0a9c1447deb30c89cc637c36","position":"1787376791600562001-bbd16ea0-610a-44f8-91d7-aa0aefb7eaa9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"40131aec90c1407fb7350c3e0f2cef1bc18e2edfdb4534423344a479f89696e4","event_uuid":"f4e88fae-3ab5-4d5f-9872-56680d4dc254","position":{"commit_sha":"e1eb55678bcc4718784bd7b35e8fc46bb917d500","position":"1787376821463550001-f4e88fae-3ab5-4d5f-9872-56680d4dc254"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"OPERATOR RULING (recorded verbatim, attributed to the operator): \"Unreadable config should result in an error.\"\n\nThe ruling issued on loveydovey-preoceanic-geese (39f8-ae7c) applies to this ticket's MCP surface too: an unreadable/corrupt rebar.toml must raise a loud error, not silently resolve gates to their defaults. So the approach here changes from 'distinguish the states, keep the safe fail direction' to 'surface the error per MCP error conventions' — config.mcp_readonly() / config.mcp_gate() must not swallow ConfigError into a default; the MCP resolvers must surface the config fault to the caller. Description will be updated with the revised design before claim, after the gate_enabled half (39f8-ae7c) lands.","timestamp":1787334526007708001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation done RED->GREEN: new module tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_unreadable_config_errors_8408.py failed 8/8 on main, passes after. mcp_readonly/mcp_gate raise ConfigError (chained, naming gate + ruling); mcp_gate fail kwarg removed as dead; _mcp_errors envelope guard + error_code_for gained config_unreadable (2045 PS4 surface-parity advisory); event-schema.md gate_unreadable text retargeted to historical-only (2045 PS4 maintainability advisory); runner_support._readonly_gate propagates. Targeted suites green (352 tests incl. held-out envelope contracts), make lint, mypy 626 files, complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0. Pushed as Gerrit change 2071 (d2c7b8640d). file_impact widened (+docs/release-notes.md, +docs/env-vars.md) — will re-run review-plan before close.","timestamp":1787376821463550001}],"created_at":1787268322778972001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"851dae7e-66a9-4d2e-98ee-5266e6ba2b2f","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"f5c4-b2d1-4503-4bfe"},{"link_uuid":"1898e1db-3afa-424e-b918-22dc56a0e52f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7e0d-7815-4425-4fdb"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nOperator ruling (recorded on this ticket and executed for the CLI/library surface in\n39f8-ae7c, merged as Gerrit change 2045 / commit 91e5ef893d): **\"Unreadable config should\nresult in an error.\"** `gate_enabled` now raises `ConfigError` on an unreadable\n`rebar.toml`, and the CLI (`main()` boundary) and library (`rebar.claim`/`rebar.transition`\ndocstrings + the `rebar.ConfigError` re-export) surface it. Two sibling resolvers in\n`src/rebar/config.py` still collapse the same config-read FAULT into the configured/default\nvalue, and the MCP adapter cannot surface the fault at all (change 2045's PS4 surface-parity\nadvisory, `src/rebar/_mcp_errors.py`):\n\n* `config.mcp_readonly()` — `except ConfigError: return True`. A broken config reads as the\n  `mcp.readonly` POLICY choice. Consumed by `mcp_server._readonly` (write-tool registration)\n  and `runner_support._readonly_gate` (comment-tool withholding).\n* `config.mcp_gate(attr, *, fail)` — `except ConfigError: return fail`. Same collapse for\n  `mcp.allow_llm` / `mcp.allow_jira_sync`, consumed by `mcp_server._mcp_gate` via\n  `_allow_llm` / `_allow_jira_sync` (per-request checks in `_mcp_llm.py` tools and\n  `_mcp_writes.py` workflow LLM-step gating).\n\nPer the ruling this is no longer \"distinguish the states, keep the safe fail direction\"\n(the pre-ruling approach below is superseded): a config fault must ERROR loudly, never\nsilently resolve to a default — even a safe one — because a fault that reads as a policy\nchoice never gets fixed.\n\n## Approach\n\nRaise at the SOURCE, mirroring the 39f8-ae7c seam exactly (one posture, one message shape):\n\n1. `config.mcp_readonly()` drops its `except ConfigError: return True`; it re-raises a\n   `ConfigError` chained `from` the parse fault, naming the gate (\"the MCP read-only gate\")\n   and citing operator ruling 39f8-ae7c, in the same message shape `gates.gate_enabled` uses.\n2. `config.mcp_gate(attr)` does the same (naming \"the mcp.<attr> gate\"). Its `fail`\n   keyword existed ONLY to pick the malformed-config fallback, so it is now dead and is\n   REMOVED; `mcp_server._mcp_gate` drops the parameter it merely forwarded, and\n   `_allow_llm` / `_allow_jira_sync` update their calls and their \"Fail-SAFE off\" comments\n   to the new error posture. (No third tri-state is minted anywhere — the pre-ruling idea\n   of reusing `GateState` is dead: `GateState` is back to a two-value policy enum and the\n   fault path is an exception, exactly as in 39f8.)\n3. MCP surfacing (the 2045 PS4 surface-parity advisory): `_mcp_errors._envelope_error`\n   adds `ConfigError` to its known-exception set, and `_errors.error_code_for` classifies\n   `ConfigError` to a NEW vocabulary code `config_unreadable` (added to\n   `KNOWN_ERROR_CODES`), so an MCP tool hitting an unreadable config returns the structured\n   envelope (machine-readable code + the parse-fault message) instead of an opaque crash.\n   The addition is additive and covered by the held-out envelope contract tests\n   (`tests/interfaces/contracts/test_mcp_error_envelope_*.py`), which pin\n   code∈`KNOWN_ERROR_CODES`.\n4. `runner_support._readonly_gate` needs no code change — the error now propagates out of\n   the shared resolver — but its \"fails CLOSED (read-only)\" docstring paragraph is\n   retargeted to the error posture.\n5. Server startup already fails closed on an unreadable config (`build_server` reads\n   composed config via `compose_config`, which propagates `ConfigError`); registration-time\n   `ctx.readonly()` propagation is consistent with that documented contract.\n6. Docs: `docs/config.md` (the mcp gate bullets' fail-direction sentences),\n   `docs/mcp-reference.md` (error-envelope vocabulary gains `config_unreadable`), and —\n   the second 2045 PS4 advisory, same ruling — `docs/event-schema.md`'s stale\n   `gate_unreadable` text (still described as \"unreadable config, gate failed open\") is\n   retargeted to: historical value only, no new write produces it, an unreadable config\n   errors per 39f8-ae7c.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/config.py` — `mcp_readonly` / `mcp_gate` raise; `fail` kwarg removed.\n- `src/rebar/mcp_server.py` — `_mcp_gate`, `_allow_llm`, `_allow_jira_sync` signature/\n  comment updates.\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_errors.py` — `ConfigError` in the envelope guard's known set.\n- `src/rebar/_errors.py` — `config_unreadable` in `KNOWN_ERROR_CODES` + `error_code_for`\n  branch (before the generic `error_code` attribute step; ConfigError carries none).\n- `src/rebar/llm/runner_support.py` — `_readonly_gate` docstring retarget.\n- `docs/config.md`, `docs/mcp-reference.md`, `docs/event-schema.md` — contract text.\n- `CHANGELOG.md` — entry under [Unreleased] (behavior change on the MCP surface).\n- Tests: retarget `tests/unit/test_config_ev3a_aliases.py`\n  (`test_mcp_readonly_fails_closed_on_malformed` → raises; the `allow_llm` garbage-env arm\n  → raises); new RED module `tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_unreadable_config_errors_8408.py`;\n  envelope-code coverage rides the existing held-out contract suites.\n\n## Testing\n\nRED before GREEN (the new module fails on current main, passes after):\n\n- Happy/failure pairs at each resolver: readable config on/off → the configured bool for\n  `mcp_readonly()` and `mcp_gate(\"allow_llm\")`; malformed `rebar.toml`/`pyproject.toml` →\n  `ConfigError` raised, chained from the parse fault, message naming the gate and the\n  ruling.\n- Consumer propagation: `mcp_server._readonly` / `_allow_llm` and\n  `runner_support._readonly_gate` propagate the typed error (no swallow anywhere on the\n  path).\n- MCP envelope: `_envelope_error(ConfigError(...))` returns an `McpEnvelopeError` whose\n  envelope carries `error == \"config_unreadable\"`; `rebar.error_code_for(ConfigError(...))\n  == \"config_unreadable\"` and the code is in `rebar.KNOWN_ERROR_CODES`.\n- Invariance guards: readable-config resolution byte-identical (file key honored, env\n  wins), existing ev3a alias tests stay green minus the two retargeted arms.\n- Full gates: `make lint`, targeted pytest for the modules above plus the held-out\n  envelope contract suites, `make typecheck`, complexity ratchet.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] With a malformed config, `config.mcp_readonly()` and `config.mcp_gate(attr)` raise\n  `ConfigError` (chained from the parse fault, message naming the gate and ruling\n  39f8-ae7c) instead of returning a bool — checked by the new\n  `test_mcp_gate_unreadable_config_errors_8408.py`.\n- [ ] The `fail` kwarg is gone from `config.mcp_gate` and `mcp_server._mcp_gate`; no\n  caller passes a malformed-config fallback anywhere — checked by grep in review and the\n  updated call sites compiling under mypy.\n- [ ] An MCP tool failing on an unreadable config yields the structured envelope with the\n  new `config_unreadable` code — checked by the new module (envelope unit arm) and the\n  held-out contract suites staying green with the enlarged vocabulary.\n- [ ] `runner_support._readonly_gate` propagates the error (no catch on the path) —\n  checked by the new module's consumer-propagation arm.\n- [ ] A readable config's behaviour is byte-identical (file key honored, env wins, both\n  policy values resolve as before) — checked by the surviving ev3a alias tests.\n- [ ] `docs/config.md`, `docs/mcp-reference.md`, and `docs/event-schema.md` state the new\n  contract (unreadable config ⇒ error; `gate_unreadable` historical-only) — checked by\n  reading the three updated sections.\n- [ ] Exactly one fault posture exists: no new tri-state enum, no second copy of\n  `GateState` — checked in review.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/config.py","reason":"mcp_readonly/mcp_gate raise ConfigError instead of collapsing to a default; fail kwarg removed"},{"path":"src/rebar/mcp_server.py","reason":"_mcp_gate/_allow_llm/_allow_jira_sync drop the fail fallback and document the error posture"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_errors.py","reason":"ConfigError joins the envelope guard known-exception set (2045 PS4 surface-parity advisory)"},{"path":"src/reba